# Prompt Reference

> Agent instructions SSOT: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) at the project root.

Use this guide to understand how each Copier prompt shapes the generated project.

## Prompt Matrix

| Prompt | Choices | Default | Description |
|--------|---------|---------|-------------|
| `project_layout` | `single-package`, `monorepo` | `{{ project_layout }}` | Lean single package or a pnpm-managed monorepo. |
| `task_runner` | `just`, `makefile`, `both`, `none` | `{{ task_runner }}` | Local task aggregator. `just` is the 2.0 default. |
| `openspec_extra` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ openspec_extra }}` | Optional OpenSpec extra files. Off by default. |
| `cli_module` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ cli_module }}` | Enables the CLI package and CLI tests. |
| `cli_languages` | `python`, `rust`, `go` (multiselect list) | `{{ cli_languages }}` | CLI implementation languages. TypeScript is MCP-only, not a CLI choice. |
| `api_module` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ api_module }}` | Master switch for HTTP APIs. |
{% if api_module == 'enabled' %}
| `api_languages` | `python`, `node`, `rust`, `go` (multiselect list) | `{{ api_languages }}` | API languages when `api_module=enabled`. Must be a YAML list. |
| `api_features` | `graphql`, `websocket` (multiselect list) | `{{ api_features | default([]) }}` | Optional API extras when `api_module=enabled`. `graphql_api_module` / `websocket_module` are derived flags, not prompts. |
{% endif %}
| `mcp_module` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ mcp_module }}` | Adds an MCP server scaffold. |
| `mcp_languages` | `python`, `typescript`, `rust`, `go` (multiselect list) | `{{ mcp_languages }}` | MCP languages. `node`/`js` remaps to `typescript`. |
| `docs_module` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ docs_module }}` | Master switch for the docs site. Disable here — `docs_framework` has no `none`. |
{% if docs_module == 'enabled' %}
| `docs_framework` | `fumadocs`, `sphinx-shibuya`, `docusaurus` | `{{ docs_framework }}` | Docs engine when `docs_module=enabled`. |
{% endif %}
| `saas_infra_module` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ saas_infra_module }}` | SaaS starter infra (was `saas_starter_module`). |
| `saas_auth_module` / `saas_auth_provider` | module toggle; provider `clerk` or `authjs` | — | Auth split dests (was `saas_auth`). `lucia` is not a dest provider and fail-closes. |
| `saas_billing_module` / `saas_billing_provider` | module toggle; `stripe` / `paddle` / `lemonsqueezy` | — | Billing split dests (was `saas_billing`). |
| `saas_admin_dashboard` | `true`, `false` | `{{ saas_admin_dashboard }}` | Admin dashboard (was `include_admin`). |
| `shared_logic` | `disabled`, `enabled` | `{{ shared_logic }}` | Shared helper modules consumed by CLI/APIs. |
| `mise.toml` | always rendered | Node **22**, Python 3.11, pnpm 9.15.0 | Generated toolchain pin. Not an extra toggle. |

## Dependency Groups

Run these as needed after enabling modules:

- **Baseline**: `uv sync`
- **Tests**: `uv sync --group test`
- **Code Quality**: `uv sync --group quality`
- **Notebooks**: `uv sync --group notebook`
- **CLI** (`cli_module=enabled`): `uv sync --group cli`
- **FastAPI** (`api_module=enabled` and `api_languages` includes `python`): `uv sync --group api_python`
- **FastMCP** (`mcp_module=enabled`): `uv sync --group mcp`

For `api_languages` containing `node`, run `pnpm install` and the relevant `pnpm --filter …` commands.

## Compatibility Notes

- Enabling `cli_module` or any `api_languages` automatically benefits from `shared_logic=enabled`.
- `project_layout=monorepo` expects pnpm and Node.js 22+. Ensure `pnpm install` is run before executing Node smoke tests.
- `docs_module=enabled` with `docs_framework=fumadocs` requires the Node toolchain; keep the Shibuya Sphinx starter as fallback when minimal environments are preferred.
